  (uuid_generate_v4(), 'handmade-indigenous-beaded-corn-earrings-ivory-seed-beads-real-corn-husks-1-5-mi', '4614104884', 'https://www.etsy.com/listing/4614104884/handmade-indigenous-beaded-corn-earrings?click_key=88861da3-e3d9-479a-bf79-3455fad45126%3ALT08be93b2c28a9e44d217ce8427ad7ee8d779e1b4&click_sum=017c1c00&ls=s&ga_order=most_relevant&ga_search_type=all&ga_view_type=gallery&ga_search_query=Navajo+jewelry&ref=search_grid-729084-8-9&sr_prefetch=1&pf_from=search&content_source=88861da3-e3d9-479a-bf79-3455fad45126%253ALT08be93b2c28a9e44d217ce8427ad7ee8d779e1b4',
   'Handmade Indigenous Beaded Corn Earrings | Ivory Seed Beads & Real Corn Husks | 1.5" Miniature Corn Earrings | Native American Beadwork', 'Title: Handmade Indigenous Beaded Corn Earrings | Ivory Seed Beads & Real Corn Husks | 1.5" Miniature Corn Earrings | Native American Beadwork Jewelry Description: 🌽 A Celebration of the Three Sisters, Ancestral Agriculture & the Sacred Gift of Corn Carry a little piece of the harvest wherever you go with these beautiful handmade Indigenous beadwork corn earrings. Measuring approximately 1.5 inches, each miniature ear of corn is lovingly crafted from shimmering ivory-colored seed beads and topped with genuine, naturally dried corn husks. Delicate gold-tone findings complete these charming earrings, blending traditional agricultural symbolism with contemporary wearable artistry. Across many Indigenous cultures, corn represents nourishment, abundance, resilience, and the enduring relationship between people and the land. As one of the Three Sisters alongside beans and squash, corn holds a cherished place in generations of Indigenous agricultural knowledge and food sovereignty. These earrings honor that living legacy through a design celebrating one of Turtle Island''s most important ancestral crops. Product Details: - Length: Approximately 1.5 inches - Bead Color: Creamy ivory - Materials: Glass seed beads, genuine dried corn husks, and gold-tone metal findings - Style: Indigenous beadwork, botanical, agricultural, harvest jewelry - Design: Miniature ears of corn with natural husk detailing - Quantity: One matching pair - Handmade: Each pair features the unique character of handcrafted beadwork and natural materials Perfect For: Indigenous fashion enthusiasts, gardeners, seed savers, agricultural educators, advocates for food sovereignty, and anyone who appreciates meaningful, nature-centered jewelry. Whether worn for a harvest celebration, cultural gathering, farmers market, or everyday occasion, these little ears of corn are a beautiful reminder that every seed carries a story. 🌽 Wear the harvest. Honor the ancestors. Celebrate the seeds that sustain us. Please not', 'turquoise-jewelry',
